#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397283 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d9576e0-3be5-5d05-8cc8-c3ecde496b46" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Solutions of Homogeneous BVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fc9b72e9-fff2-5f3d-af71-a6cc5a8690e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397285} {:answer/id #uuid "e0887495-5b99-519d-8b06-b050d9a2f259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397286} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecfede9-c62d-5886-a299-f1a637666f1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397287}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fc9b72e9-fff2-5f3d-af71-a6cc5a8690e6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397285} :answer-field/id #uuid "0c637c93-1ee3-58ef-993c-3c6e5c1fc84b" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397284} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b52e930-14ea-531b-b526-eaff6b0fb8cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397289} {:answer/id #uuid "8afc5730-0411-589a-b64a-42f650c93db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6}(3{e}^{4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397290} {:answer/id #uuid "6b215d5b-71fa-5321-b766-c19abcce664a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6}(3{e}^{3}+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397291} {:answer/id #uuid "db7b6416-a35a-5ac4-84e2-f2ecee72c7f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397292} {:answer/id #uuid "cd306ca1-9609-57f9-8243-6c8325a1cf83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397293}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8afc5730-0411-589a-b64a-42f650c93db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6}(3{e}^{4}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397290} :answer-field/id #uuid "33bba31b-5240-5dae-836f-d5e2781c4733" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397288} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dcc04b9a-9cfc-5141-a860-86088f43169c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397295} {:answer/id #uuid "3900c0eb-6950-53f9-bfb1-9594df80a763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det(A)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dcc04b9a-9cfc-5141-a860-86088f43169c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397295} :answer-field/id #uuid "40ecf88c-bee2-552d-9e9b-2221a6455c26" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397294} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f04959b-3b97-5dd8-8bc1-66c4bf84b779" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-3x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397298} {:answer/id #uuid "55749b1e-7fb0-5999-951d-ee88ea733318" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{3x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397299} {:answer/id #uuid "a7af3aac-e800-5201-888a-579b4e28c609" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397300} {:answer/id #uuid "de01c055-6b53-5e7e-b43f-8cad2dcffec0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397301}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55749b1e-7fb0-5999-951d-ee88ea733318" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{3x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397299} :answer-field/id #uuid "abb190aa-1853-5191-97ba-08809006a2a4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397297}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76fbcb9f-680c-51b9-b052-efdce55007dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-338982" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+3y=0,\\,y(1)={y}^{′}(3)=0,\\,1\\le x\\le 3\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(3) & {y}_{2}^{′}(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem has a unique solution if and only if {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}(x)+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$   \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have Robin boundary conditions given by\n\n$$\ny(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(3)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, setting ${\\alpha }_{1}=1,$ ${\\beta }_{1}=0,$ ${\\alpha }_{2}=0,$ ${\\beta }_{2}=1,$ and $a=1,$ $b=3,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}(1) & {y}_{2}(1) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(3) & {y}_{2}^{′}(3)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-4m+3 & =0 \\\\ (m-1)(m-3) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have ${m}_{1}=1$ and ${m}_{2}=3,$ and so the fundamental solutions are\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x}\\,\\text{and}\\,{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=3{e}^{3x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1} & {e}^{3(1)} \\\\ {e}^{3} & 3{e}^{3(3)}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}e & {e}^{3} \\\\ {e}^{3} & 3{e}^{9}\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =e(3{e}^{9})-{e}^{3}({e}^{3}) \\\\  & =3{e}^{10}-{e}^{6} \\\\  & ={e}^{6}(3{e}^{4}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has the unique solution }y≡0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01c5809f-cb10-5192-b646-13036813137d" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems Using Integrating Factors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c73a7b2-a2bf-518a-beb1-31fbbadf0c5c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397304} {:answer/id #uuid "d70f278f-f71b-563b-90a5-a72e4490f97d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397305} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9aa96a-e438-54ed-91f2-a9cd9b89c2af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{6{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397306} {:answer/id #uuid "be7b681a-d4b7-5605-ba2e-22acaaed6363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}+5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397307} {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397308}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e0d3cd9-78d0-5801-b268-5ffd73ca96c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397308} :answer-field/id #uuid "40c6d291-cf90-51ae-b2e3-e5400146213f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397303} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e829349-3bd7-53b1-81eb-45b5da9870a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{12x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397310} {:answer/id #uuid "ddaeb121-e0a6-501b-9a51-af6c7d17b5d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397311} {:answer/id #uuid "831b7918-1f4b-50de-b1bd-28a0091624cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397312} {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397313}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "327e9b36-504a-55cd-bdeb-9a295dbac872" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397313} :answer-field/id #uuid "f1cc20f5-acca-5b79-8f90-bd4ac033d4c7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397309}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b18cb65d-b781-5075-91bf-6c656ac3ed30" :question/math-academy-id "q-339145" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y=x,\\,y(0)=5\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options below.\n$\\,$ An integrating factor for this equation is $I(x)=$ {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The solution to the initial value problem is $y(x)=$ {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "This equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)y=Q(x),\n$$\n\nwith $P(x)=\\frac{x}{6}$ and $Q(x)=x.$\n\nWe compute an integrating factor using the definition:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (x/6)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the equation in standard form by $I(x)={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}y) & ={e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot x \\\\ {e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{x}{6}{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\cdot y & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}) & =x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x,$ making use of the substitution $u=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{12}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12})\\text{d}x & =\\int x{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =\\int 6{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{u}+C \\\\ y{e}^{{x}^{2}/12} & =6{e}^{{x}^{2}/12}+C \\\\ y & =6+C{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis is the general solution. To find the value of $C$ corresponding to the specific solution, we apply the initial condition $y(0)=5$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =6+C{e}^{-{0}^{2}/12} \\\\ 5 & =6+C \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=6-{e}^{-{x}^{2}/12}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397314 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96494014-7289-548b-9749-2eb6336c9cef" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Solutions of Inhomogeneous BVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e79a7021-331e-58f2-b8f6-85a889c84c54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397316} {:answer/id #uuid "5cf42a17-28d9-5cef-872e-d088f9b14525" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397317} {:answer/id #uuid "0b68a318-1bc5-51d1-9c23-3a3907eceead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397318} {:answer/id #uuid "299cc599-8438-5e31-a5d0-214b9d59050d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397319} {:answer/id #uuid "198c8e7f-e98a-5eaf-a800-18f9ff78792b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397320}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "299cc599-8438-5e31-a5d0-214b9d59050d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397319} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3c520b4-13a5-571c-8e5c-ab4db2ff4923" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397315} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b599fd4e-bc9d-5170-a7bb-6d77f919c9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397322} {:answer/id #uuid "386da076-43fa-52ac-a62c-687b10effaa2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397323} {:answer/id #uuid "4d473d8d-facd-578f-bf7b-b27f7e42de91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397324}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b599fd4e-bc9d-5170-a7bb-6d77f919c9df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397322} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9682d6c-ccfb-538a-ad04-e49378c99e16" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397321} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c2ba89f2-d45a-52ff-863e-45c304e0008e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397326} {:answer/id #uuid "aa418ebb-9208-5e1f-9afb-0bfc91434063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has at most one solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397327} {:answer/id #uuid "1e77e3f6-6e5a-5fea-9d66-fcd13e99bf41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has a unique solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397328} {:answer/id #uuid "e9b6382a-3196-58ad-b56a-9f2fd256cf92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions or no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397329}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa418ebb-9208-5e1f-9afb-0bfc91434063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has at most one solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397327} :answer-field/id #uuid "34be03c6-2aad-5ef1-bef0-db216fa83c72" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397325}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "dfa31998-de06-5abd-90a7-06def4c1434e" :question/math-academy-id "q-339169" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+y=x{e}^{3x},\\,{y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0,\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & {y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & {y}_{2}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below **without calculating the solution** to this BVP. \n\n$\\,$ The **absolute value** of $det(A)$ is {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the corresponding homogeneous BVP {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, our inhomogeneous BVP {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order inhomogeneous boundary value problem (BVP)\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $P,Q,$ and $f$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i}$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nThe inhomogeneous BVP has at most one solution if and only if the associated homogeneous BVP has only the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Specifically:\n\n- If the homogeneous BVP has the unique solution $y≡0,$ then the inhomogeneous problem either has no solution or a unique solution.\n\n- If the homogeneous BVP has (infinitely many) nontrivial solutions, then the inhomogeneous problem either has infinitely many solutions or no solution.\n\nTo classify the solutions of the corresponding homogeneous BVP, we define the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ In other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the homogeneous BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have Neumann boundary conditions. So, setting ${\\alpha }_{i}=0,{\\beta }_{i}=1,a=0,$ and $b=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & {y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & {y}_{2}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm \\text{i}.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,{y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\ -sin\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2})\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(A)| & =|0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot (-1)| \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the corresponding homogeneous BVP $\\text{has the unique solution }y≡0.$\n\nTherefore, since the corresponding homogeneous BVP has the unique solution $y≡0,$ our inhomogeneous BVP $\\text{has at most one solution}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397330 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96494014-7289-548b-9749-2eb6336c9cef" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Solutions of Inhomogeneous BVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14a56e84-f444-514c-b047-407709ef1b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397332} {:answer/id #uuid "7cc1070d-440b-55d7-89c6-dad455f0b8ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3}-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397333} {:answer/id #uuid "cca250e3-057e-56c3-aa82-f205a90f5f76" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397334} {:answer/id #uuid "160196c4-affe-5ba6-9053-25ce0b327293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397335} {:answer/id #uuid "0daa7d71-da3c-5c32-8b51-686cd74886cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397336}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "160196c4-affe-5ba6-9053-25ce0b327293" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e-\\frac{1}{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397335} :answer-field/id #uuid "87a4bdb6-3e46-5b30-beb9-78c8ccdca610" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397331} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bda6fc1-48eb-5196-9d91-5862f18707e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397338} {:answer/id #uuid "71878905-3b4f-5678-aa10-771a1c34b5f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397339} {:answer/id #uuid "2c628e4f-1497-597b-b3da-f70cc3a170fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bda6fc1-48eb-5196-9d91-5862f18707e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397338} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5c70429-c9c1-5e9c-a93f-75d9d38f18f1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397337} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6637efb4-ea3e-50db-8daf-d770124713cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397342} {:answer/id #uuid "3f17e337-89d2-5e4c-9b71-670eca2cb748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has at most one solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397343} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b01b12-4d13-5495-bae2-fcf7ff5dcf54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has a unique solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397344} {:answer/id #uuid "33b326e7-0527-59c6-b429-eed05129d540" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions or no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f17e337-89d2-5e4c-9b71-670eca2cb748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has at most one solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397343} :answer-field/id #uuid "70c9fd63-30e4-560e-89a6-edd2f7d51959" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397341}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "302bac11-c0dd-5a24-97f7-11c22c2ff5b5" :question/math-academy-id "q-339173" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-y={x}^{2}{e}^{x},\\,{y}^{′}(0)={y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & {y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(1) & {y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below **without calculating the solution** to this BVP. \n\n$\\,$ The **absolute value** of $det(A)$ is {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, the corresponding homogeneous BVP {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, our inhomogeneous BVP {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order inhomogeneous boundary value problem (BVP)\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x),\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)={\\gamma }_{1},\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)={\\gamma }_{2}\n$$\n\nwhere $P,Q,$ and $f$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i}$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ \n\nThe inhomogeneous BVP has at most one solution if and only if the associated homogeneous BVP has only the trivial solution $y≡0.$ Specifically:\n\n- If the homogeneous BVP has the unique solution $y≡0,$ then the inhomogeneous problem either has no solution or a unique solution.\n\n- If the homogeneous BVP has (infinitely many) nontrivial solutions, then the inhomogeneous problem either has infinitely many solutions or no solution.\n\nTo classify the solutions of the corresponding homogeneous BVP, we define the matrix $A$ as\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe homogeneous BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$ In other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the homogeneous BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have Neumann boundary conditions. So, setting ${\\alpha }_{i}=0,{\\beta }_{i}=1,a=0,$ and $b=1,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & {y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ {y}_{1}^{′}(1) & {y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=\\pm 1.$ So, the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)={e}^{x},\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=-{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{0} & -{e}^{0} \\\\ {e}^{1} & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ e & -{e}^{-1}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(A)| & =|1\\cdot (-{e}^{-1})-(-1)\\cdot e| \\\\  & =-{e}^{-1}+e \\\\  & =e-\\frac{1}{e}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)\\ne 0,$ the corresponding homogeneous BVP $\\text{has the unique solution }y≡0.$\n\nTherefore, since the corresponding homogeneous BVP has the unique solution $y≡0,$ our inhomogeneous BVP $\\text{has at most one solution}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397346 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7d9576e0-3be5-5d05-8cc8-c3ecde496b46" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Solutions of Homogeneous BVPs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5540be47-9b2a-568d-be51-652a02adfb88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397348} {:answer/id #uuid "d678551d-3097-5de2-b1cc-a3e1a6bcdb5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16{e}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397349} {:answer/id #uuid "9db1d09d-e694-5e62-ab53-9c17dbbeb79b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4({e}^{2}-{e}^{-2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397350} {:answer/id #uuid "accf96b7-4aa5-51ca-911b-0609fc4e4c1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4({e}^{2}+{e}^{-2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397351} {:answer/id #uuid "448f7af0-31e0-552a-b83c-766dbceb2915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397352}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "448f7af0-31e0-552a-b83c-766dbceb2915" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397352} :answer-field/id #uuid "07191edc-8ad7-5bb9-946e-ceccac633b37" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397347} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05c19e3e-7994-55a5-b3fd-d6b53f5e6b97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397354} {:answer/id #uuid "225ba7d1-c5d6-5cd7-9a9d-2fcb8a221e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-2x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397355} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc877a8-9ed9-5862-8ad6-a3cde7bb3319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{-2x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)=x{e}^{-2x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397356} {:answer/id #uuid "16c47780-a095-51a6-87af-0eeac027f5f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{4x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "225ba7d1-c5d6-5cd7-9a9d-2fcb8a221e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}$ and ${y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-2x}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397355} :answer-field/id #uuid "31c9adde-b1e2-5899-93ea-5c224e70de0f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397353} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "026c0ee9-634f-5e06-8e57-216dd4b78ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397359} {:answer/id #uuid "c5e299b9-8db8-5c7c-930c-76867c68e4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det(A)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397360}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "026c0ee9-634f-5e06-8e57-216dd4b78ca8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "det(A)\\ne 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397359} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c72e2c4-74c9-59b4-8573-f0cc3090072c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7b62cf72-f57f-5f0d-9158-aef592b88ff9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has the unique solution $y≡0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397362} {:answer/id #uuid "3e1123ab-1573-54ff-beeb-fb38fc921c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397363} {:answer/id #uuid "cfc3748e-f6bb-54fa-bdd2-c9d309081222" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has no solution" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3e1123ab-1573-54ff-beeb-fb38fc921c64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "has infinitely many solutions" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397363} :answer-field/id #uuid "e53b80d8-ad34-5531-b34b-01b41813b9b4" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397361}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "355bfeb1-d0b8-53cd-b763-3f92856140f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-339176" :question/problem "Consider the following boundary value problem (BVP).\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-4y=0,\\,2y(0)-{y}^{′}(0)=2y(1)-{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x)$ be the fundamental solutions, and suppose we define the matrix $A$ as \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}(0)-{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & 2{y}_{2}(0)-{y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ 2{y}_{1}(1)-{y}_{1}^{′}(1) & 2{y}_{2}(1)-{y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFill in the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\n$\\,$ The boundary value problem has a unique solution if and only if {{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The fundamental solutions to this BVP are {{field-2}}.\n\n$\\,$ For this BVP, we have $det(A)=$ {{field-3}}.\n\n$\\,$ Therefore, this BVP {{field-4}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have the second-order homogeneous boundary value (BVP) problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}(x)+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,a\\le x\\le b\n$$\n\nwith the Robin (mixed) boundary conditions\n\n$$\n{\\alpha }_{1}y(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}^{′}(a)=0,\\,{\\alpha }_{2}y(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}^{′}(b)=0\n$$\n\nwhere $P$ and $Q$ are continuous on $[a,b],$ and ${\\alpha }_{i}$ and ${\\beta }_{i}$ are real constants such that $({\\alpha }_{i},{\\beta }_{i})\\ne (0,0).$ Furthermore, suppose the fundamental solutions to the equation are ${y}_{1}(x)$ and ${y}_{2}(x).$ \n\nNow, let's define the following matrix:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\,{\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{1}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{1}^{′}(a) & {\\alpha }_{1}{y}_{2}(a)+{\\beta }_{1}{y}_{2}^{′}(a) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{1}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{1}^{′}(b) & {\\alpha }_{2}{y}_{2}(b)+{\\beta }_{2}{y}_{2}^{′}(b)\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, the BVP has a unique, trivial solution $y≡0$ if and only if $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nIn other words, if the determinant equals zero, then the BVP has *infinitely many solutions*.\n\nNotice that, in our case, we have mixed (Robin) boundary conditions. So, setting ${\\alpha }_{i}=2,$ ${\\beta }_{i}=-1,$ $a=0,$ and $b=1,$ the matrix $A$ reduces to\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2{y}_{1}(0)-{y}_{1}^{′}(0) & 2{y}_{2}(0)-{y}_{2}^{′}(0) \\\\ 2{y}_{1}(1)-{y}_{1}^{′}(1) & 2{y}_{2}(1)-{y}_{2}^{′}(1)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the fundamental solutions, we set $y={e}^{mx}.$ The auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}^{2}-4 & =0 \\\\ (m-2)(m+2) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have $m=2$ and $m=-2,$ and so the fundamental solutions are \n\n$$\n{y}_{1}(x)={e}^{2x}\\text{ and }{y}_{2}(x)={e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n{y}_{1}^{′}(x)=2{e}^{2x},\\,{y}_{2}^{′}(x)=-2{e}^{-2x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix $A$ is\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4{e}^{-2}\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nand we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =0(4{e}^{-2})-0(4) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(A)=0$ we conclude that this BVP $\\text{has infinitely many solutions }.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640be27-8277-5a9c-bf14-83bcc7a38604" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of Inhomogeneous ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "de93b087-2c87-54a2-8ce4-861cedbe5c5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397367} {:answer/id #uuid "38b22569-4620-5db6-9463-291c3a777e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "38b22569-4620-5db6-9463-291c3a777e54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397368} :answer-field/id #uuid "bcb669d8-5345-5c4e-b897-7495dd431c78" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397366} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52998750-f1d9-5a19-9002-6bfcf31c55e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{4}+B{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397370} {:answer/id #uuid "e45559f1-ba00-51cc-b081-a77f686eee2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{3}+B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397371} {:answer/id #uuid "5002b657-e4ab-5c5f-89fb-7b1998744e13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{3}+Bx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397372} {:answer/id #uuid "9978a706-bbf5-5974-83fc-49c20b94ddc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{2}+Bx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397373}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e45559f1-ba00-51cc-b081-a77f686eee2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{3}+B" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397371} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4a1bd78-53d2-516c-8d40-e476d527e8c3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397369} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31cf0eda-a4b6-57d7-b68f-8800d2cddce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397375} {:answer/id #uuid "001536f4-f360-5cf9-a291-5a9b1f3dfd29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397376}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31cf0eda-a4b6-57d7-b68f-8800d2cddce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397375} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dd92b7c-9494-5d4d-a0bf-2c6eb063c6ff" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397374} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "195c6c70-aac6-5801-900c-371891911ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397378} {:answer/id #uuid "c81b4ebd-b840-598a-aa24-ae2dde79292a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "195c6c70-aac6-5801-900c-371891911ecc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397378} :answer-field/id #uuid "01df666f-a411-5cb8-a769-1be13f346ebd" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397377} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cfacfd88-65dc-5834-aa27-53751d867ede" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397381} {:answer/id #uuid "f70ffe80-4c54-5c5e-bd95-d1c6101ae78d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397382} {:answer/id #uuid "f0077fa3-42e5-59ab-a09b-eca6c457084d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397383} {:answer/id #uuid "9eeef3cd-9631-5a88-85c7-a19c1d56b153" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397384}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0077fa3-42e5-59ab-a09b-eca6c457084d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397383} :answer-field/id #uuid "2e06630b-2bf3-51a2-895d-741decfb22bb" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397380}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "af1eb49f-2047-54c5-af74-dcf0eb0576e3" :question/math-academy-id "q-339910" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}=-2x\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{3}+B,$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." :question/worked-solution "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}=1, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(1)^{′}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(0)-2x(1)=-2x.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{2})^{′}=2x, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(2x)^{′}=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(2)-2x(2x)=-2x.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{2}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{3}+B.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{x}^{3}+B+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7640be27-8277-5a9c-bf14-83bcc7a38604" :knowledge-point/title "Constructing General Solutions of Inhomogeneous ODEs"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f61fa9d-029d-5d0b-836f-7fd9c52c55bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397387} {:answer/id #uuid "89a0b1c8-9210-56e2-99b9-b8e5988b2240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397388}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89a0b1c8-9210-56e2-99b9-b8e5988b2240" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397388} :answer-field/id #uuid "609fd564-70da-56dd-9299-95878b1b6445" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397386} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81058251-1165-5c9f-ab12-5cfd387d4523" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{4}+B{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397390} {:answer/id #uuid "a47b03cd-dfc7-52e9-8092-bfa976cb5cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{3}+Bx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397391} {:answer/id #uuid "5e8be5da-3d82-55a6-a528-4cbcd7fd1d12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397392} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1768c0-d2ed-570a-84f8-b83dd61715fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f1768c0-d2ed-570a-84f8-b83dd61715fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397393} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e38af75-4659-57c3-acc3-d958cb168075" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397389} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ff04874c-b806-5c51-8ff8-c7783a6dee7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397395} {:answer/id #uuid "3d3314f6-149b-5289-97b2-4076da38e6a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397396}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ff04874c-b806-5c51-8ff8-c7783a6dee7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$A$ and $B$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397395} :answer-field/id #uuid "93034832-63fb-5330-ae88-5be7fabc5ce3" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397394} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e591a31f-a1bb-5d07-9267-8c626c839c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397398} {:answer/id #uuid "478f5c4d-a4a2-5d7e-9928-ff87d28d0d95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "is" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e591a31f-a1bb-5d07-9267-8c626c839c91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "isn't" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397398} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc5e5305-f978-5920-9dc9-d9d702e1ab1a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397397} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f417bc71-5d41-5c9e-beba-54bc27b5b30c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397401} {:answer/id #uuid "26af1e26-5364-554f-8e28-c0d8d4ea85a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397402} {:answer/id #uuid "254b41b3-fead-5a42-8ab3-af055f04dd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397403} {:answer/id #uuid "8e9bf666-0e4e-52c1-995e-f94b6aabf304" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{x}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397404}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "254b41b3-fead-5a42-8ab3-af055f04dd2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397403} :answer-field/id #uuid "db42da3c-4ff8-55e8-8bd3-19b8e3c4c33c" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397400}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4f873b9e-7818-5ec8-8091-26b92885da7b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339913" :question/problem "$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}-6x{y}^{′}+10y=4x\n$$\n\nConsider the differential equation above, for which the corresponding complementary solution is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{2},$ where $A$ and $B$ are arbitrary constants. Select the correct options below.$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)=x$ \n{{field-1}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe function ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{3}$ \n{{field-2}} \na particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$\nThe general solution of the differential equation is given by\n\n$\\,\\,$\n$y(x)=$ \n{{field-3}}\n$+$\n{{field-4}},\n\n$\\,$\nwhere \n{{field-5}} are arbitrary constants." :question/worked-solution "For an inhomogeneous differential equation, the general solution is given by\n\n$$\ny(x)={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x),\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}_{c}(x)$ is the complementary solution (the general solution of the corresponding homogeneous equation), and\n\n- ${y}_{p}(x)$ is a particular solution of the original inhomogeneous equation.\n\nWith this in mind, let's check which of the two given functions is a particular solution of our inhomogeneous equation:\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)=x,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}=1, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(1)^{′}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(0)-6x(1)+10(x)=4x.\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)=x$ $\\text{is}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\n- For ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{3},$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =({x}^{3})^{′}=3{x}^{2}, \\\\ {y}^{″}(x) & =(3{x}^{2})^{′}=6x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the equation, we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}(6x)-6x(3{x}^{2})+10({x}^{3})=4x.\\,\\,\\times \n$$\n\nSo, ${y}_{p}(x)={x}^{3}$ $\\text{isn't}$ a particular solution of the differential equation.\n\nWe are told that the complementary solution of our equation is ${y}_{c}(x)=A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{2}.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & ={y}_{c}(x)+{y}_{p}(x) \\\\  & =A{x}^{5}+B{x}^{2}+x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $A\\text{ and }B$ are arbitrary constants."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167288 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2236311d-1dcf-5814-8621-6ca58ac136e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397406} {:answer/id #uuid "80766049-c81a-5e17-9add-d24c5e9a61f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397407} {:answer/id #uuid "9c2a205e-e06c-5302-98bb-33dd8ef28f57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397408} {:answer/id #uuid "74af64a7-831f-50b9-989b-da92fb9efa80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397409} {:answer/id #uuid "47abc435-93f1-5e56-be4e-2906875645c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397410} {:answer/id #uuid "84fdd6c1-2fa1-53ec-9f4e-f2c79cf04198" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2236311d-1dcf-5814-8621-6ca58ac136e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397406} :answer-field/id #uuid "41c0a54b-4090-5079-ad72-a367200f1bb8" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397405} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "576de101-4a4e-5d10-93f1-4794297dd084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397413} {:answer/id #uuid "8be2ea60-7536-54c6-8c40-2b3ca7f53e09" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397414} {:answer/id #uuid "ebd3c9f2-b034-51ed-b959-1917ee861c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397415} {:answer/id #uuid "a0938cb1-fa06-51a3-9682-a27947461754" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397416} {:answer/id #uuid "16682102-e4e9-5e8e-b234-f5f85ae7a7c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397417}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebd3c9f2-b034-51ed-b959-1917ee861c61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397415} :answer-field/id #uuid "acd80bdd-4dbe-5452-b9e2-03bec982eb3d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397412} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6896852-8238-5500-8785-a40ba1143f26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397419} {:answer/id #uuid "7f0541cc-7371-58fe-8dca-eb545f614b78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397420} {:answer/id #uuid "610883b1-a3e9-5606-b9ae-cf0dd1218917" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397421} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3717c9-e1f6-51ef-9d7f-0c5c74af7ae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397422} {:answer/id #uuid "23137492-fa85-5ebf-bdf6-f3faffc43cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "23137492-fa85-5ebf-bdf6-f3faffc43cb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397423} :answer-field/id #uuid "d466e0c2-5e9a-5545-9677-019c4fb5c4a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397418}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "aa20d8e3-c4d9-5112-bd9c-ec30f6aaa6fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-340418" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{2}$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{5}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{5} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(10x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{20}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{20}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(10\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-10\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ & ={a}_{5}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{5} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{5} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397424 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8748773f-b48a-58ec-b951-7e2f13629f66" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397426} {:answer/id #uuid "0e3eeb27-01e0-5659-a89f-03c69d0adcb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397427} {:answer/id #uuid "c5615bd6-2ce4-5da1-a40b-3086abdcadd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397428} {:answer/id #uuid "07510649-4bdf-56eb-8d9c-ed267705e564" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397429} {:answer/id #uuid "03be0b57-cf22-512e-a317-32a2b0abe9aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397430} {:answer/id #uuid "c2a9dc62-5426-5219-b618-40a8ef37dfaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397431}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5615bd6-2ce4-5da1-a40b-3086abdcadd8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397428} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b23de8e-d2ee-5400-a7e2-b5cd4049a1e7" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397425} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "603a374f-5ef4-515c-9c7e-fa8563eb145a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397433} {:answer/id #uuid "bdb3a316-1e8b-5c4e-88ed-2cc1c3a89e42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397434} {:answer/id #uuid "e2451042-dca2-5c68-9e00-de451ff94150" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397435} {:answer/id #uuid "aeaacf6b-f6f1-598e-9735-a55707c901f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397436} {:answer/id #uuid "54e98588-ab60-5ad4-b62c-cc9eebe7a31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aeaacf6b-f6f1-598e-9735-a55707c901f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397436} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc891073-56d2-5c57-9375-2988eb59d895" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397432} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44414e5e-ea6c-5e29-8c97-658e69445da6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397439} {:answer/id #uuid "4e818916-b8da-55ed-9e45-159ab74b3b1c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397440} {:answer/id #uuid "fef36346-1430-5b7e-8f8d-dbd4ef5452d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397441} {:answer/id #uuid "681611df-aafb-58e2-b2fd-60ed1c5a8c81" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397442} {:answer/id #uuid "dca82b61-b202-5c4b-8b2a-4f67990862a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397443}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dca82b61-b202-5c4b-8b2a-4f67990862a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397443} :answer-field/id #uuid "d98a60af-8b0a-5156-82e3-3b9f66208118" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397438}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "df849e8a-df1b-5b2f-bbc1-5b6e2ad9aeb2" :question/math-academy-id "q-340638" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{3}+5x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{6}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{6} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(12x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{24}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\pi -(-\\pi ))-\\frac{1}{24}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-12\\pi ))) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ & ={a}_{6}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{6} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{3}+5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397444 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5211e103-bbae-56b5-ab1d-86eeee675e89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397446} {:answer/id #uuid "549261c0-0dda-5beb-b854-9f2f8b637398" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397447} {:answer/id #uuid "eeadf2f7-53bd-5a77-9e67-80289734e565" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397448} {:answer/id #uuid "a2c627de-a8e3-50ae-9a5e-cacf82786e25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397449} {:answer/id #uuid "6787651e-aa4d-5093-84e5-d0a95f255245" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397450} {:answer/id #uuid "f34b9fe5-933e-5b07-9848-aa70bc7a0b18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2c627de-a8e3-50ae-9a5e-cacf82786e25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397449} :answer-field/id #uuid "4484c5be-bfb9-56e1-91bb-68d4eb55bee1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397445} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "676fc215-8323-51e6-b8c4-0af2d1a3be4c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397453} {:answer/id #uuid "2a944a6e-5a73-58dd-9364-1a3d02c8c7c7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397454} {:answer/id #uuid "c916f828-527d-56b1-a7f4-05bfb34ceabb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397455} {:answer/id #uuid "64e9ee42-0c88-535d-bada-848d67fb20fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397456} {:answer/id #uuid "03257e03-c6ac-58ac-bb14-ad066e5d197b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397457}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c916f828-527d-56b1-a7f4-05bfb34ceabb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397455} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c16f558-7e63-5623-83b7-64f167dc11d9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2023ddfa-d889-50c9-878f-85d10c84ea35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397459} {:answer/id #uuid "50c89892-3614-52d6-882b-bc4708a1c3b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397460} {:answer/id #uuid "ac65746c-c51f-545e-b99a-4117e9bf4102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397461} {:answer/id #uuid "b5530228-de94-5b2c-b5a7-3602545b76b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397462} {:answer/id #uuid "57843cbf-6acc-57b7-b1e7-b524e63e1320" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397463}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5530228-de94-5b2c-b5a7-3602545b76b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397462} :answer-field/id #uuid "a1d13c1c-619d-5f29-9d08-2c83813e46e8" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397458}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "13f82e1b-2f3e-536a-8bb2-1fc6ddf6b76a" :question/math-academy-id "q-340645" :question/problem "Let $F(x)={x}^{4}-7x$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{3}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{3} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that is piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n{a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{cos}^{2}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{2}x+\\frac{1}{12}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(2\\pi -0)-\\frac{1}{12}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(12\\pi )-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ & ={a}_{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩ \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)⟩} \\\\ {a}_{3} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }({x}^{4}-7x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397464 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c086bc97-415d-52c9-b26a-02dc8aebef33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Trigonometric and Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6154e534-d5aa-500e-a111-0642cb1f5138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397466} {:answer/id #uuid "90e7fe06-494b-5336-8647-cec5893e79b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397467} {:answer/id #uuid "62aa5026-98f2-56d7-9078-cf1f425f67e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397468} {:answer/id #uuid "309debb7-997b-556d-8512-eacab65daa9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397469} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cdc23e-3f2e-58ea-8f36-763705ca4acc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397470} {:answer/id #uuid "0da6a2a1-bbda-52c4-af89-8ae0dc014a0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6154e534-d5aa-500e-a111-0642cb1f5138" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397466} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fe74c7f-d29a-5023-a627-6b99c33c73b4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397465} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c12b77e-d15a-5d68-b82e-75459493d093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397473} {:answer/id #uuid "375df8b6-49b7-502b-a948-207f0f617763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397474} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e087e4-24d7-5ffa-92ca-31063530bd9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3s}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397475} {:answer/id #uuid "e24a7d49-39e9-59b8-a286-404d727d74eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397476} {:answer/id #uuid "8608c77e-449a-5d7d-bd75-65fa63256437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8608c77e-449a-5d7d-bd75-65fa63256437" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397477} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dfa2d25-b9ae-5bb9-b792-43292f1be3e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397472}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "42bf59e6-fc11-5187-a3f2-889c117ed67e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340655" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)=\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}+{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-3t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3},\\,s>3 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3},\\,s>-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{3t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-3t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-3}+\\frac{1}{s+3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+3)+(s-3)}{(s-3)(s+3)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (3,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-3t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-3,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(3,\\infty )\\cap (-3,\\infty )=(3,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fadf4f64-3569-56b2-98e1-f6681892054a" :knowledge-point/title "Checking Orthogonality of Sines and Cosines"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8433c533-4904-5d92-885f-bbcd959dd940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397480} {:answer/id #uuid "7f4020d2-476a-5794-a6f2-3d8b125330ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are not orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8433c533-4904-5d92-885f-bbcd959dd940" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "are orthogonal" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397480} :answer-field/id #uuid "199c37d6-b74a-50da-a86e-fce04acf3561" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397479} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "deda8e08-d6bd-5e0e-ae0c-00112e17523f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397483} {:answer/id #uuid "4d231c1e-d79b-5508-b44e-84b13e3b138c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397484} {:answer/id #uuid "2134b48b-4f80-54ce-97ca-e2ded504ec18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397485} {:answer/id #uuid "dfbe5295-15de-5429-ac7d-1288d0b2be34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2134b48b-4f80-54ce-97ca-e2ded504ec18" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397485} :answer-field/id #uuid "4ea71ffc-f171-5611-bfc4-d57724eb7008" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397482}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d6ca311-b229-51f5-b6ee-b805697465fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-340669" :question/problem "$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nGiven the inner product on the set of continuous functions over $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ defined above, select the correct options below.$\\,$\n$⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩=$ \n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,$\nThe functions $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Evaluating the inner product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x),1⟩ & ={\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)]}_{-\\pi }^{\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6\\pi )-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-6\\pi )) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{6}(1-1) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x)$ and $g(x)=1$ $\\text{are orthogonal}$ with respect to the inner product."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397487 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "532a73e6-e026-57c9-9bad-57cd2f75b6df" :knowledge-point/title "Parity Recognition and Series Type"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d6fb8e02-c2ed-54c2-a769-c0f5e618e887" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "even" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397489} {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397490}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "82f2576e-7f7d-514c-b7d3-b07f1e9d3631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "odd" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397490} :answer-field/id #uuid "35a58589-56cd-5637-b523-03f859fac5b6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397488} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34d21a9d-340e-5cb4-a005-7da885a8f606" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "sine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397492} {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397493}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1b091b7e-9971-5f89-be72-b0882bfa2d62" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "cosine terms" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397493} :answer-field/id #uuid "52a06cf5-506a-5aec-8bcd-ea5d4fda8897" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397491}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8afd30f6-9418-5f9f-a8dd-bdb05d34a03e" :question/math-academy-id "q-340806" :question/problem "Consider the function $f(x)={x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)$ on $x\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ].$ Select the correct options below.\n$\\,$\nThe function $f(x)$ is\n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$\nConsequently, the \n{{field-2}}\nin the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x)$ must be zero." :question/worked-solution "To determine whether $f$ is even or odd, we compare $f(-x)$ and $f(x):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(-x) & =(-x)^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-x) \\\\  & =-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) \\\\  & =-f(x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(-x)=-f(x),$ we have that $f$ is odd.\n\nFor Fourier series on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ],$ the cosine coefficients are given by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)\\,\\text{d}x,\n$$\n\nand the constant coefficient is\n\n$$\n{a}_{0}=\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nHere, $f(x)$ is odd and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is even, so $f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)$ is odd. Also, $f(x)$ itself is odd.\n\nNow, the integral of an odd function over $[-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ is $0.$ Thus, ${a}_{n}=0$ for all $n\\ge 1,$ and ${a}_{0}=0.$\n\nTherefore, the function $f(x)$ is $\\text{odd}$ and the $\\text{cosine terms}$ in its Fourier series must be zero."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397494 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "8ec39e02-0c39-5aa4-90e2-3477259d6262" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Step Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d80295e-b463-5e7c-bf1a-e7d0d9f86058" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397496} {:answer/id #uuid "08ab9610-98a7-5832-b2b7-84ed96b7fb63" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397497} {:answer/id #uuid "660727ef-7b2d-531b-8658-07e77f29dd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "660727ef-7b2d-531b-8658-07e77f29dd8e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397498} :answer-field/id #uuid "3811f53b-a1af-5f49-ab19-7ecfb660367f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e77341d6-4bd5-508f-b10c-e6b1abd62aa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{5{e}^{-5s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397500} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd85fe4-dc49-5e10-8a3c-4aae5e0e97e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397501} {:answer/id #uuid "5a60055f-03ee-5493-96d8-f946458ffa97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397502} {:answer/id #uuid "ec6b9f59-ce56-5db4-9460-84a4cfcd9c8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{5{e}^{-5s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397503} {:answer/id #uuid "ab7ef87a-673e-59b2-8d9c-a72764dc0faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397504}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab7ef87a-673e-59b2-8d9c-a72764dc0faa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397504} :answer-field/id #uuid "3311ff79-3ee4-524b-acee-81bb9dd688cc" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397499}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "94c1a445-854c-59cd-8bb7-f1e99e5361c5" :question/math-academy-id "q-340883" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)}$ for $f(t)=u(t-2)+u(t-5),$ where $u$ is the unit step function.$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the unit step function is defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<0 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise functions $u(t-2)$ and $u(t-5),$ we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u(t-2) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 2\\end{aligned} \\\\ u(t-5) & ={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<5 \\\\ 1,\\, & t\\ge 5.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nu(t-2)+u(t-5)={\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & t<2 \\\\ 1,\\, & 2\\le t<5 \\\\ 2,\\, & t\\ge 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for our Laplace transform, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}0\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{2}^{5}1\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the second integral diverges for $s\\le 0.$\n\nFor $s>0,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{5}^{\\infty }2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{2}^{5}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{5}^{a}{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s}]}_{2}^{5}+2{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(-\\frac{{e}^{-st}}{s})|}_{5}^{a} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{-sa}-{e}^{-5s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}-\\frac{2}{s}(0-{e}^{-5s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}-\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}+\\frac{2{e}^{-5s}}{s} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $f(t)$ is\n\n$$\nL{f(t)}=\\frac{{e}^{-2s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-5s}}{s},\\,s>0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186222031 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e48d92fd-eb5d-54d5-8a5a-8eba48db736d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397506} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a91d3a-6b36-5a0c-8213-9c8a1b4a253c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397507}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e48d92fd-eb5d-54d5-8a5a-8eba48db736d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397506} :answer-field/id #uuid "aec337f7-4ecf-50fc-9a79-93502b4464a2" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397505} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "018f92a0-3544-5274-a50b-8ab59d99d148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397509} {:answer/id #uuid "8da1c6b9-b712-5f96-ba6a-7e76dc3b56a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397510}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "018f92a0-3544-5274-a50b-8ab59d99d148" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397509} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fdcb018-a1ac-541a-9916-1b8c916a43a1" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397508} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cf7a93f0-2cfa-5048-9f86-bb34deaaea7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397512} {:answer/id #uuid "d7341562-4fa3-5103-b7de-023d18a018f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397513}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf7a93f0-2cfa-5048-9f86-bb34deaaea7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397512} :answer-field/id #uuid "6bb56a2a-394d-574e-ad3d-34e850271acd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397511} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fff6d535-67cf-5d92-a24c-282ed886a3f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397515} {:answer/id #uuid "13360f60-446f-5ba5-8fe4-4db596852ca9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397516}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fff6d535-67cf-5d92-a24c-282ed886a3f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397515} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecd037f3-14ce-5899-ac94-7cf1fd33f9d0" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2cc2bb4c-12ce-5499-9381-7f752bdaab23" :question/math-academy-id "q-341129" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}, & x\\in [0,3) \\\\ -3x, & x\\in [-3,0)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-3,3).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-3,3).$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/18/186106373f9848cfefefb23197e7508497ff3d570f326da2ca342d078682128d.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{true}.$ The function $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-3,3).$ It consists of two smooth pieces.\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{true}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}-3x=-3(-3)=9\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}{x}^{2}=(3)^{2}=9.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{3}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {3}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{true}$ since statements I, II, and III are all true.\n\n**Note:** The $6$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/89/89c3a597ce1114fee9e775f291cf89e8ca04f61eb39cf2b4c896dd4be8022f09.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397517 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c086bc97-415d-52c9-b26a-02dc8aebef33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Trigonometric and Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a145f15c-ceb4-50f6-84e5-8b7834619199" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397519} {:answer/id #uuid "29c9ba6e-cb4a-511a-a3e8-afa19fa0cd85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397520} {:answer/id #uuid "a538529b-1b93-5744-80c9-65509cce8a2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397521} {:answer/id #uuid "651aadd0-1e95-54cb-96ff-254e6eef8952" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397522} {:answer/id #uuid "871991e0-f1d8-558e-90c5-5f962efd70eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397523} {:answer/id #uuid "3aaeac27-3d73-5c9c-86eb-0838799cd60f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397524}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "871991e0-f1d8-558e-90c5-5f962efd70eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397523} :answer-field/id #uuid "4550c540-2a81-570b-87fb-628f14326571" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397518} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ee99e0c-d4c4-5917-b998-b7dec7f37dcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397526} {:answer/id #uuid "2bb3ed42-d158-5ad8-af7f-d31ff6b6b3c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397527} {:answer/id #uuid "4a13a688-1c5e-567d-bb42-ea175ded90cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397528} {:answer/id #uuid "7aac7682-f32b-5b3d-b4d4-32d39a154d58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}-16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397529} {:answer/id #uuid "88396452-9be4-582b-b646-fd6f295eadb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397530}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88396452-9be4-582b-b646-fd6f295eadb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397530} :answer-field/id #uuid "b87144df-013d-5d61-8a79-c97d52888b76" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397525}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "db14dea0-146d-5df5-a79a-6c50bf00be55" :question/math-academy-id "q-341136" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that the cosine function can be defined in terms of complex exponentials as follows: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)=\\frac{{e}^{4\\text{i}t}+{e}^{-4\\text{i}t}}{2}\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4\\text{i}t}+{e}^{-4\\text{i}t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4\\text{i}t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-4\\text{i}t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4\\text{i}t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-4\\text{i}t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{4\\text{i}t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-4\\text{i}t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}}=\\frac{1}{s-\\text{i}\\omega },\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4\\text{i}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-4\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+4\\text{i}},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{4\\text{i}t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-4\\text{i}t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-4\\text{i}}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+4\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-4\\text{i}}+\\frac{1}{s+4\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+4\\text{i})+(s-4\\text{i})}{(s-4\\text{i})(s+4\\text{i})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}+16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndefined for $s>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397531 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c086bc97-415d-52c9-b26a-02dc8aebef33" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Trigonometric and Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "461b0ac0-5211-5e64-aa63-d08093e5e804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397533} {:answer/id #uuid "a7b6b192-ec4b-5aca-a7e5-b7e2362c242a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8s}{{s}^{2}-64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397534} {:answer/id #uuid "992044c1-c091-557f-b232-73069b3560a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}+64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397535} {:answer/id #uuid "2e13c630-4b5b-5b09-ab98-ae7663e336b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397536} {:answer/id #uuid "e26f2812-efee-58e1-bc49-fa54b5fa6464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}-64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e26f2812-efee-58e1-bc49-fa54b5fa6464" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}-64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397537} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e065cee-e495-59be-a49b-48b465530e20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397532} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "758b98a0-94c0-5be6-b097-b85d31f91123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397539} {:answer/id #uuid "91240e34-abfd-5826-835b-a95cbbd93c8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397540} {:answer/id #uuid "c1c6fc60-0e73-5a81-8093-d5c8cfec9a2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge -8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397541} {:answer/id #uuid "93d7be6d-9a7a-59df-b1e3-a5deb3df60a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397542} {:answer/id #uuid "3942e53b-efa0-5e2e-aeb2-41186bd71234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397543} {:answer/id #uuid "9f65ca28-dfe3-5a9c-8051-5e8c9de202af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397544}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91240e34-abfd-5826-835b-a95cbbd93c8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397540} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d76374-c302-5673-ab25-1a0eb5568341" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397538}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f89dc302-60ce-5bd9-b567-660590ce563f" :question/math-academy-id "q-341140" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)=\\frac{{e}^{8t}-{e}^{-8t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}-{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{8t}}{2}}-L{\\frac{{e}^{-8t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{8t}}-\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-8t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{8t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-8},\\,s>8 \\\\ L{{e}^{-8t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+8},\\,s>-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{8t}}-\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-8t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-8}-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+8} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-8}-\\frac{1}{s+8}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+8)-(s-8)}{(s-8)(s+8)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{16}{{s}^{2}-64}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{{s}^{2}-64}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{8t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (8,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-8t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-8,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(8t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(8,\\infty )\\cap (-8,\\infty )=(8,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>8.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "304c015d-cbb6-5989-a102-d6f0f5f38604" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Expressions For Fourier Coefficients"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d7d31a3-b2e8-5955-b7a5-8d0265e34185" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397547} {:answer/id #uuid "14f752d4-26f3-5b55-951a-267514a31272" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397548} {:answer/id #uuid "86ecc11d-d361-56e3-b985-f0af7df41e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397549} {:answer/id #uuid "3ecabd1c-c6be-5ae6-a083-97bdd6237c82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397550} {:answer/id #uuid "b23326b9-dc50-5189-864f-580f0beb25f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b23326b9-dc50-5189-864f-580f0beb25f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397551} :answer-field/id #uuid "40e8826c-c720-5c71-8e60-9efc9028ee9f" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397546} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "74b0c5c0-5b9c-5ca0-a3b8-c0e23762591f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397553} {:answer/id #uuid "037567f7-c39a-5a21-9477-5930025ede7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397554} {:answer/id #uuid "5a2e6cae-f02e-5650-9bdf-362d1f1fa2b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397555} {:answer/id #uuid "64699d60-b695-59b3-84f5-62b93bdee4e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397556} {:answer/id #uuid "4c59d8f0-ecad-5bf2-9285-f977292bfdcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4c59d8f0-ecad-5bf2-9285-f977292bfdcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\pi }" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397557} :answer-field/id #uuid "df14591b-b6cc-5cdd-adc7-9dbfe95edc2a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397552} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cd7a6256-c073-5d27-93a0-6184aec661c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397559} {:answer/id #uuid "e3d09424-4779-58cb-a9a8-a20b503a58f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397560} {:answer/id #uuid "fd0b285c-99a5-5dc6-b53e-349ca170a4bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397561} {:answer/id #uuid "d6de7f97-87a8-587c-be9e-52648a5b0102" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨f(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}{⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397562} {:answer/id #uuid "330f62f3-2b9c-5888-9cec-d52701d82d24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{⟨1,1⟩}{⟨f(x),1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397563}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd0b285c-99a5-5dc6-b53e-349ca170a4bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397561} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e635cb7-5fb0-5dc2-9345-111ede6d51d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397558}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "73b220ad-78ed-5227-b775-ed2065f7b0fd" :question/math-academy-id "q-341308" :question/problem "Let $F(x)=3x+1$ for $x\\in R,$ and let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of $F$ from $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ to $x\\in R.$ The Fourier series of $f$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)).\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the expression for the coefficient ${a}_{0}$ below, where $⟨\\,,⟩$ denotes the usual inner product on functions over $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{0} & ={{field-1}} \\\\  & ={{field-2}}\\,\\cdot \\,{{field-3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The usual inner product of functions $f$ and $g$ over $x\\in [0,2\\pi )$ is given by\n\n$$\n⟨f(x),g(x)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)g(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFor a $2\\pi $-periodic function $f(x)$ that's piecewise continuous over $x\\in [0,2\\pi ),$ the Fourier series of $f$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)∼\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),\n$$\n\nwhere ${a}_{0},$ ${a}_{n},$ and ${b}_{n}$ are constants to be determined. \n\nNow, we find the inner product of $f(x)$ with $1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }({a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)+{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)),1⟩ & = \\\\ ⟨\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2},1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }⟨{b}_{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩ & = \\\\ \\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx),1⟩+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{b}_{n}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx),1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the functions\n$1,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x),\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x),\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x),…$\nare orthogonal with respect to the defined inner product, the only nonzero term in the final expression above is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩.\n$$\n\nComputing the inner product, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨1,1⟩ & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[x]}_{-0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =2\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨f(x),1⟩ & =\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}⟨1,1⟩ \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{2⟨f(x),1⟩}{⟨1,1⟩} \\\\ {a}_{0} & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\pi }\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(3x+1)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397564 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "424fc261-d1ca-5bf0-b085-7af1de6cc7cc" :knowledge-point/title "Finding Laplace Transforms of Other Piecewise Continuous Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04fdc9fb-cd44-5e0e-b22f-8f67fce82a51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397566} {:answer/id #uuid "cabe113f-508f-5a0e-ae94-fc0083b16c13" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397567} {:answer/id #uuid "0cc99fcc-e772-5e94-b870-35a9db5a4ba3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397568} {:answer/id #uuid "a6ae2c3f-920d-5b6e-8987-c30c8599133a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397569} {:answer/id #uuid "d4a6dad1-27fa-519f-81f0-cc70bb51b3f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397570} {:answer/id #uuid "99f28136-fb56-52a1-98a2-8be91b7068aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4a6dad1-27fa-519f-81f0-cc70bb51b3f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s>1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397570} :answer-field/id #uuid "a55cae0b-d0e7-5c92-b5d3-5cd9673f9f43" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397565} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61ae7223-aa34-5db5-aa66-4e5fde9de0ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(s-1)}}{s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397573} {:answer/id #uuid "b0648719-f6f1-5582-a9c7-b2e40208d75c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397574} {:answer/id #uuid "ce80b731-5ad8-572d-9659-a7d36ed14cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397575} {:answer/id #uuid "edaa60e1-e666-514b-893d-b9aec909db8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397576}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce80b731-5ad8-572d-9659-a7d36ed14cbd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397575} :answer-field/id #uuid "87e3c7a6-fbb4-5070-994b-44c52d38d82f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397572}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d8e97793-b7f7-5bb2-8257-c5344e5ddb06" :question/math-academy-id "q-341448" :question/problem "Use the definition of Laplace transforms to calculate $F(s)=L{f(t)},$ where $f(t)$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}2,\\, & t\\le 3 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\, & t>3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$\\,F(s)=L{f(t)}=$ {{field-1}},\nvalid for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "We apply the definition of the Laplace transform:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{f(t)} & =F(s)={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(t)={\\begin{aligned}2,\\, & t\\le 3 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\, & t>3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }f(t){e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{t}\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2\\cdot {e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{t-st}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the improper integral diverges if $s\\le 1.$\n\nFor $s>1,$ we calculate our Laplace transform as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(s) & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{e}^{-st}\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{s}{[{e}^{-st}]}_{0}^{3}+{\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{3}^{a}{e}^{(1-s)t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+{lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{(\\frac{{e}^{(1-s)t}}{1-s})|}_{3}^{a} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{1-s}\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }({e}^{(1-s)a}-{e}^{3(1-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{1}{1-s}\\cdot (0-{e}^{3(1-s)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{s}-\\frac{2{e}^{-3s}}{s}+\\frac{{e}^{3(1-s)}}{s-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nvalid for $s>1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124867 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "71f8b1c9-7856-52fa-8990-a83fda9ef2a9" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying Points for a Differential Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42d4e07a-aa53-5b14-88a3-04309d900d01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397578} {:answer/id #uuid "80394f18-b738-54ac-9c5e-5b5f1497c047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397579} {:answer/id #uuid "2c3b1e62-fd12-53e6-a2e6-437965ed144c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397580}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "80394f18-b738-54ac-9c5e-5b5f1497c047" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397579} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b0b6010-a8e4-5818-9b9e-07b9fa2156c5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397577} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bbed6fca-b1b4-5cb5-a628-05c2a2876f25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397582} {:answer/id #uuid "f6c04487-b3e1-54a8-91d4-f475965ddee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397583} {:answer/id #uuid "d23321d7-6d21-5e82-b71a-8df7426c4beb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397584}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bbed6fca-b1b4-5cb5-a628-05c2a2876f25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397582} :answer-field/id #uuid "27f98080-0f8c-5167-a519-b69c9b9da579" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397581} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "121b342d-94a4-5a32-b807-9fd677a437eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397586} {:answer/id #uuid "006f2dab-a7ef-56db-8b52-1e8b65fff7ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397587} {:answer/id #uuid "deca4897-4c3e-5bad-9f24-155edaba92f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397588}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "deca4897-4c3e-5bad-9f24-155edaba92f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397588} :answer-field/id #uuid "b18cd1f9-4635-565b-9f81-413f7fa8c5bf" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397585} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ae1974be-cae5-5a5c-b85c-da80cb6ca3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397590} {:answer/id #uuid "a8e73a36-ba65-5180-ab1b-3d21c5dd5547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an ordinary" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397591} {:answer/id #uuid "ec690560-1681-5c8e-9a5e-d9729f1a5cb8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "a regular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae1974be-cae5-5a5c-b85c-da80cb6ca3f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "an irregular singular" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397590} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4dc4c18-d716-57a7-86b8-c7cc062be0ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397589}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9c2710b8-4c49-5de2-8583-5f8c80fe5c91" :question/math-academy-id "q-342410" :question/problem "$$\nx(x-3)(x+1){y}^{″}+(x-3){y}^{′}+x(x+1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y=0\n$$\n\nClassify the following points for the differential equation given above.$\\,$The point $x=-1$ is\n{{field-1}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=0$ is\n{{field-2}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=2$ is\n{{field-3}}\npoint of the differential equation.\n\n$\\,$The point $x=3$ is\n{{field-4}}\npoint of the differential equation." :question/worked-solution "The point $x=a$ is an ordinary point of the differential equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=f(x)\n$$\n\nif both $P(x)$ and $Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, $x=a$ is a singular point of the differential equation.\n\nA singular point $x=a$ is regular if both $(x-a)P(x)$ and $(x-a)^{2}Q(x)$ are analytic about $x=a.$ Otherwise, the singular point is irregular.\n\nFirst, we rewrite the differential equation in standard form by dividing by $x(x-3)(x+1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(x-3)(x+1){y}^{″}+(x-3){y}^{′}+x(x+1)(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)y & =0 \\\\ {y}^{″}+\\frac{1}{x(x+1)}{y}^{′}+\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-3}y & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nP(x)=\\frac{1}{x(x+1)}\\,\\text{and}\\,Q(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nThe function $P(x)$ is *not* analytic about points where $x(x+1)=0,$ which occurs at $x=0$ and $x=-1.$\n\nThe function $Q(x)$ is *not* analytic about points where $x-3=0$ or where $\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is undefined. These occur at $x=3$ and $x\\le 0.$\n\nTherefore, $x=2$ is $\\text{an ordinary}$ point of the differential equation, and the singular points are\n\n$$\nx=-1,\\,x=0,\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nNow, let's classify each singular point.\n\n- For $x=-1,$ the function\n\n$$\n(x+1)P(x)=(x+1)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x(x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=-1,$ and the function\n\n$$\n(x+1)^{2}Q(x)=(x-1)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-3},\n$$\n\nis undefined about $x=-1.$ So, $x=-1$ is $\\text{an irregular singular}$ point of the differential equation.\n\n- For $x=0,$ the function\n\n$$\nxP(x)=x\\cdot \\frac{1}{x(x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x+1},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=0,$ but the function\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}Q(x)={x}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-3},\n$$\n\nis undefined about $x=0.$ So, $x=0$ is $\\text{an irregular singular}$ point of the differential equation.\n\n- For $x=3,$ the function\n\n$$\n(x-3)P(x)=(x-3)\\cdot \\frac{1}{x(x+1)},\n$$\n\nis analytic about $x=3,$ and the function\n\n$$\n(x-3)^{2}Q(x)=(x-3)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x-3}=(x-3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nis also analytic about $x=3.$ Therefore, $x=3$ is $\\text{a regular singular}$ point of the differential equation."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397593 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2ae32a2a-438f-547c-8510-7e9f760c3cb6" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Properties of Periodic Extensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8755164a-0677-56b8-a14a-88ef64412325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397595} {:answer/id #uuid "fd07ffa2-060b-5390-8c1e-f3fa7f05b91e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd07ffa2-060b-5390-8c1e-f3fa7f05b91e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397596} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2cb40da-a7f4-5c99-8c06-a63a258898b3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397594} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f672220a-3d44-5a57-9dc4-f393d21fd036" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397598} {:answer/id #uuid "778d4e9c-9ed6-508e-89cf-bb2d161c14a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "778d4e9c-9ed6-508e-89cf-bb2d161c14a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397599} :answer-field/id #uuid "37025846-4756-5f39-9aec-cf0c7c1f7476" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397597} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "96826b32-74fa-517b-814f-48bf8e8d6576" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397601} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ba36c9-f2ba-565a-b1c4-51749cec3189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f2ba36c9-f2ba-565a-b1c4-51749cec3189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397602} :answer-field/id #uuid "c95a34df-dd3f-5841-9258-36788f5137b0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397600} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a784da2-d4e4-5d4b-b900-c6ed1e90fed0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "True" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397604} {:answer/id #uuid "4b07bc9b-8163-5605-b7bf-f62facb32b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4b07bc9b-8163-5605-b7bf-f62facb32b99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "False" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397605} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b046f21-736c-5f03-a92f-dec58bf868ea" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397603}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "24b6f004-4c8b-5565-a4ef-1d172930ca34" :question/math-academy-id "q-342657" :question/problem "$$\nF(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+2, & x\\in [-2,0] \\\\ \\frac{1}{x}, & x\\in (0,2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe above function $F(x)$ is defined on $x\\in [-2,2).$ Let $f(x)$ be the $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R.$\nSelect the correct options below.\n\n| I. | $F(x)$ is continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-1}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| II. | $F(x)$ is piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ | {{field-2}} |\n| III. | ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)$ | {{field-3}} |\n| IV. | $f(x)$ is piecewise smooth and continuous on $R$ | {{field-4}} |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine the given statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not continuous on $x\\in (-2,2)$ because $\\frac{1}{x}\\to \\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$ Its graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/8e/8e5eec10427a7061a05c0bd1228ce1146234bf2b09d75bb86ba83b28fbe178d9.png)\n\n- Statement II is $\\text{false}.$ The function $F(x)$ is not piecewise smooth on $x\\in (-2,2)$ because ${F}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to {0}^{+}.$\n\n- Statement III is $\\text{false}.$ Indeed, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}(x+2)=-2+2=0\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}\\frac{1}{x}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nSo, ${lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}F(x)\\ne {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}F(x).$\n\n- Statement IV is $\\text{false}$ since statements I and II are false.\n\n**Note:** The $4$-periodic extension of $F(x)$ to $x\\in R$ has the graph shown below.\n\n![](images/4a/4afcdf86f777b9c7afc8af31b36cde4b80cfe394fd908db1ccd47ef48dff1617.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "06fedec8-5aed-52f9-bd4f-aa81b9180ad4" :knowledge-point/title "Solving First-Order Initial Value Problems With Sinusoidal Forcing"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "488da8c0-0995-59d5-a5c6-54b8e67769d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s-4}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397608} {:answer/id #uuid "a55e62b5-e47d-5336-b8b7-276e9c1dbb68" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s+4}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397609} {:answer/id #uuid "f47e74e2-4bce-5a44-817d-59bd1c489c8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397610} {:answer/id #uuid "02cd391d-9944-5308-bbce-ea584369dba1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397611} {:answer/id #uuid "79c67eea-4e83-584e-9efc-0ea95542dae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "79c67eea-4e83-584e-9efc-0ea95542dae5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397612} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c237e54-7764-534a-9c54-8baed4a37d20" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2225ade3-5bf4-52e8-bb8f-84401c8e6e34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{s+2}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397614} {:answer/id #uuid "9a61bdd8-3d2f-572c-91f5-833d4e189e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}-\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397615} {:answer/id #uuid "4d73190f-40e0-562b-8571-039c42b83caf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s+2}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397616} {:answer/id #uuid "d6087e3e-f080-5ae6-bb69-2acbb87ff902" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}+\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397617}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a61bdd8-3d2f-572c-91f5-833d4e189e88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}-\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397615} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8f001e5-aaed-5c9c-a1ac-1f1aa18ef7db" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397613} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "24c20f35-2312-5896-8f00-c76ef490da78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}+\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397619} {:answer/id #uuid "287b1162-26e2-52bb-99aa-815c269f399d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2t}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397620} {:answer/id #uuid "a3aed227-d2f9-59e8-8313-76d8cc49a807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397621} {:answer/id #uuid "7e56b7cb-60e3-5844-8de1-228ec8842538" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t+\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397622}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3aed227-d2f9-59e8-8313-76d8cc49a807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397621} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e35ac8d-bb69-5204-8ed0-7880d0ca6330" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397618}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1873e66d-b721-525d-8ac0-7b13c3d92c58" :question/math-academy-id "q-342960" :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}t}+2y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,y(0)=0\n$$\n\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below to find the solution using Laplace transforms. You may make use of the following results:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{\\omega }{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nLet $Y(s)=L{y(t)}.$ Taking the Laplace transform of both sides of the equation and solving for $Y,$ we have\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nThe partial fraction decomposition of $Y$ is\n\n$$\nY(s)={{field-2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny(t)={{field-3}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, we take the Laplace transform of both sides of the differential equation. Using the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\nL{{y}^{′}}+2L{y}=L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}-L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the transform of a derivative $L{{y}^{′}}=sY(s)-y(0)$ and the standard trigonometric transforms\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t}=\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16},\\,L{\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16},\n$$\n\nwe substitute the known values. Note that $y(0)=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(sY(s)-0)+2Y(s) & =\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}-\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16} \\\\ (s+2)Y(s) & =\\frac{4-s}{{s}^{2}+16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe rearrange to solve for $Y(s).$ Dividing by $(s+2),$ we obtain\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}.\n$$\n\nNext, we perform a partial fraction decomposition. Since the denominator has a linear factor $(s+2)$ and an irreducible quadratic factor $({s}^{2}+16),$ we write\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-s}{(s+2)({s}^{2}+16)}=\\frac{A}{s+2}+\\frac{Bs+C}{{s}^{2}+16}.\n$$\n\nTo find the constants, we clear the denominators:\n\n$$\n4-s=A({s}^{2}+16)+(Bs+C)(s+2)\n$$\n\n- Setting $s=-2,$ we have\n \n\n$$\n4-(-2)=A((-2)^{2}+16)+0\\,⟹\\,6=20A\\,⟹\\,A=\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the coefficients of ${s}^{2},$ we have\n  \n\n$$\n0=A+B\\,⟹\\,0=\\frac{3}{10}+B\\,⟹\\,B=-\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Comparing the constant terms, we have\n \n\n$$\n4=16A+2C\\,⟹\\,4=\\frac{48}{10}+2C\\,⟹\\,C=-\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nThus, the decomposition is\n\n$$\nY(s)=\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}+\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{10}s-\\frac{2}{5})}{{s}^{2}+16}=\\frac{3}{10(s+2)}-\\frac{3s+4}{10({s}^{2}+16)}.\n$$\n\nFrom the table of Laplace transforms, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}} & ={e}^{-2t} \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ {L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, taking the inverse Laplace transform of $Y(s),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =\\frac{3}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{1}{s+2}}-\\frac{3}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+16}}-\\frac{1}{10}{L}^{-1}{\\frac{4}{{s}^{2}+16}} \\\\ y(t) & =\\frac{3}{10}{e}^{-2t}-\\frac{3}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t-\\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397623 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "734fe467-57d6-5b3f-a61e-1e2e4624b5fc" :knowledge-point/title "Using Abel's Identity to Conclude Independence/Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "304d5117-ee46-5c5d-afa7-ca920f029e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397625} {:answer/id #uuid "ae08826c-6c1c-5987-ad7e-864c4360f574" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397626} {:answer/id #uuid "b83dbcc8-f9de-571f-b680-6fc8b19ba9d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for some but not all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "304d5117-ee46-5c5d-afa7-ca920f029e8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x\\in R$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397625} :answer-field/id #uuid "622cd65e-d7fb-587b-8c10-1defb970706b" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397624} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ef66bf4-a759-5faa-bbe6-c8479e7aca1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4Q(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397629} {:answer/id #uuid "07f88880-7512-5cb1-85f0-9acaa96748b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397630} {:answer/id #uuid "ecd7fc4f-0bb8-5d15-9606-f2346f18bdfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397631} {:answer/id #uuid "52543647-4678-5589-9673-644a893cea31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4Q(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397632}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecd7fc4f-0bb8-5d15-9606-f2346f18bdfc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397631} :answer-field/id #uuid "80ef2068-6b95-504c-8d87-420eff7181f4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397628} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e8310ce-fbd3-5538-b766-45d5514898c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397634} {:answer/id #uuid "e082f656-48a6-5575-b482-8353f60d9a9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "Cx" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397635} {:answer/id #uuid "1d0a044d-7c2c-5bb4-bfbf-18edf83e4c37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397636} {:answer/id #uuid "b96d58ae-2f44-580e-81fa-71567a86ef0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b96d58ae-2f44-580e-81fa-71567a86ef0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{4x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397637} :answer-field/id #uuid "70866db8-d47c-5d65-8fab-fa76cb30f2a9" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397633}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "65f6d9f7-7688-5460-b686-2b9904fe578a" :question/math-academy-id "q-343289" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(0)=-1.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(0)=-1,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=-4.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=4W(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =4W \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =4\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int 4\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =4x+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{4x} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(0)=-1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(0) & =C{e}^{4\\cdot 0} \\\\ -1 & =C\\cdot 1 \\\\ C & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)=-{e}^{4x}$ and $W(x)\\ne 0\\text{ for all }x\\in R.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "734fe467-57d6-5b3f-a61e-1e2e4624b5fc" :knowledge-point/title "Using Abel's Identity to Conclude Independence/Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d90121c9-177f-56cb-abef-4c63bdbede7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397640} {:answer/id #uuid "513bee4c-d7a9-5b9d-8a90-fb020c324ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{{e}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397641} {:answer/id #uuid "912232e2-b616-5b37-bd1b-5a8f05973914" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{C}{{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397642} {:answer/id #uuid "17aa114d-1675-5b0a-92ea-b1131bf9c02e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397643}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17aa114d-1675-5b0a-92ea-b1131bf9c02e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "C{e}^{-{x}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397643} :answer-field/id #uuid "12e79a8a-77ce-5206-ad24-806b35c154fb" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397639} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f5325b4-2c7f-510a-836c-8d30b25fc79f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for some but not all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397645} {:answer/id #uuid "f7a00866-c222-5cf7-8082-6ea525338ab3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)\\ne 0$ for all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397646} {:answer/id #uuid "2c1bd3d6-1ec9-5357-b88e-6e77f2e5915e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c1bd3d6-1ec9-5357-b88e-6e77f2e5915e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$W(x)=0$ for all $x>0$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397647} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab8824e-5b62-51f7-bcc4-ce3c21af44e9" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397644} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fac610d4-aa9e-59b8-b9b1-3082677c09d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x}{Q(x)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397649} {:answer/id #uuid "aea7672b-d42a-5cb9-abad-b947e31b87bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397650} {:answer/id #uuid "f9a49da1-ba65-5fd3-9e45-8c74fb4bd158" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2xQ(x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397651} {:answer/id #uuid "86e3e6c4-6ee0-562c-b132-7062dfe19170" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397652}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aea7672b-d42a-5cb9-abad-b947e31b87bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397650} :answer-field/id #uuid "d476b0bc-73ec-5b5c-aed8-1c9dde581b2e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186397648}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4acb3708-3f85-57a1-975e-b6f23d95dbae" :question/math-academy-id "q-343293" :question/problem "$$\n{y}^{″}+2x{y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\\,x>0\n$$\n\nLet ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ be solutions to the second-order homogeneous differential equation above, where $Q(x)$ is continuous on $(0,\\infty ).$ The Wronskian satisfies $W(2)=0.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\nThe Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies the following first-order differential equation:\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)={{field-1}}W(x)\n$$\n\nSolving this equation, we get\n\n$$\nW={{field-2}}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow, using the fact that $W(2)=0,$ we obtain \n{{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Abel's identity says that if ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}$ are solutions of\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+P(x){y}^{′}+Q(x)y=0,\n$$\n\nthen their Wronskian $W(x)$ satisfies\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-P(x)W(x).\n$$\n\nIn our equation, the coefficient of ${y}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\nP(x)=2x.\n$$\n\nSubstituting into Abel's identity gives\n\n$$\n{W}^{′}(x)=-2xW(x).\n$$\n\nNow, we solve the first-order differential equation for $W:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{W}^{′} & =-2xW \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =-2x\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{\\text{d}W}{W} & =\\int -2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|W| & =-{x}^{2}+K \\\\ |W| & ={e}^{K}{e}^{-{x}^{2}} \\\\ W & =C{e}^{-{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is a constant.\n\nNext, we use the given value $W(2)=0$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}W(2) & =C{e}^{-{2}^{2}} \\\\ 0 & =C{e}^{-4} \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $W(x)=0\\text{ for all }x>0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186397653 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "734fe467-57d6-5b3f-a61e-1e2e4624b5fc" :knowledge-point/title "Using Abel's Identity to Conclude Independence/Dependence"}] :question/answer-fields [{:ans